after being sworn in by king willem  alexander prime minister margaret starts  his fourth term in office rita is the  longest-serving european leader together  with victor orban from hungary and  nearly the longest-serving prime  minister in dutch history he have to  give us the feeling that  he is the old one but it is a new era  with new ideas  and with  maybe with with  with to try  to be again  connected with the people can you do  that  i don't know that's a big question  the netherlands has become increasingly  polarized since the start of the  pandemic with nearly weekly  anti-government protests dozens of  protesters held a rally during the  cabinet inauguration the first issue on  the agenda is to regain trust research  shows that trust in politics politicians  and state institutions has gone down  from 70 percent to 29 percent in the  past year the main question is now can  the same prime minister and the same  coalition parties win this back  after british government was forced to  resign early last year the new cabinet  looks very much the same as the old one  but instead of putting a cap on spending  this one aims to allocate billions of  dollars to climate policies and housing  and aims to be more pro-european many  dutch voters aren't impressed  i think it will be the same as last  so if if the prime minister stays it  stays the same  totally nothing i don't expect anything  at all it can't get any worse than it is  already the main frustration is the way  the government has handled the covet  pandemic compared to other european  nations the netherlands has strict  lockdown measures in place with public  places shops and restaurants closed due  to high infection rates and a late start  of the booster campaign what i  experience in the netherlands is a  political leadership that really follows  the trends in society rather than leads  it it seems that in the netherlands  looking at the polls and looking at the  sentiment in the in in the in the  population is more important  for your political decisions in the next  three weeks  than really having a vision and leading  the population to that vision while many  hope that this government will offer a  long-term vision to handle the pandemic  the current lockdown which is in place  until the end of this week will most  likely be extended step faster al  jazeera the hague
 

